        "identifier": "PALOMAR-2026-10-21-000005",
        "note": "The Heath-Brown 1985 entry of this repository proves, among other results, that the even numbers that are not a sum of two primes have density zero. That classical statement is the case A = all primes of Theorem 1.2; this entry does not register it again as a compared theorem. Both entries use the lab's Siegel-Walfisz theorem.",
        "relationship": "other"
      },
